## What you may change

- Restructure headings and tables: one `##` heading per phase, one task table per phase.
- Rename columns to the canonical names (ID, Task, Deps, Status, Model, Owner, Mode, Verify, Timeout, Context); keep any other column as it is.
- When a column named Verify, Timeout or Context holds something igris would misread (a command under Verify, an estimate like `2 days` under Timeout, prose under Context), give it another name so it stays an extra column (e.g. `Verify notes`), and mention it in `## Adapt notes`.
- Normalize statuses to `ready`, `blocked`, `in progress`, `done` or `skipped`.
- Convert prose dependencies ("after the parser", "needs 2 and 3") into task IDs or ID ranges.
- Turn prose that waits on something outside the plan ("waits on", "after the client…", "blocked by deploy") into a `user` task naming the blocker (e.g. `X-00 · **Wait for API keys from client** · user · —`) and add it to the Deps of the waiting task. Mention each one in `## Adapt notes`.
- Keep non-task content (introductions, legends, notes) as plain sections without a task table.

## What you must not change

- Don't invent, guess or change models. Map a model only when the original names it unambiguously (e.g. "Claude Opus" → `opus`).
- Keep the Verify, Timeout and Context columns and their cells as written. Don't add these columns or fill a cell the original leaves empty: never invent a verify profile, a timeout or a context path, and never put a command in a Verify cell (commands live in the owner's `igris.toml`). A Verify cell naming a profile that isn't listed above stays as it is; list it in `## Adapt notes`.
- Don't drop, merge, split or reorder tasks, and don't add new ones, except the blocker tasks above.
- Don't rewrite descriptions: the Task cell keeps the original wording (escaping a `|` as `\|` is fine).
- Don't change task IDs. If a task has no ID or a duplicate one, ask the owner.

## Missing or unknown models

Give every agent task whose model is missing or doesn't map to a rank above Model `?`. `igris check` rejects `?`, so the owner fills these in after accepting. List each of them in a final section at the very end of the proposal:

```markdown
## Adapt notes

- M1-03: no model in the original
- M2-01: unknown model "gpt-4"
```

Use the same section for anything else the owner should check (columns you guessed, prose dependencies you interpreted, blocker tasks you added). Leave it out when there's nothing to note.

## Finish

Ask the owner in this chat when anything is unclear and wait for the answer. Before finishing, check the proposal with

```
igris check --plan {{.ProposalFile}}
```

and fix every problem it reports except the `?` models. When `{{.ProposalFile}}` is complete, run this as your very last action:

```
{{.DoneCommand}} --note "<one-line summary of the conversion>"
```

